1
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:11,140
Brighten up the room and take a step back,
will you?

2
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:42,860
It'll all work out somehow, eventually.

3
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:59,880
Anyone without a job, come to my place.

4
00:00:59,880 --> 00:01:04,520
I don't have one either, so don't worry.

5
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:11,560
Look, even the steel is burning.

6
00:01:13,440 --> 00:01:18,260
It'll all work out somehow, eventually.

7
00:01:20,380 --> 00:01:23,540
You get it, right? Got it, got it.

8
00:01:23,540 --> 00:01:27,380
Once you understand, shut up and follow me.

9
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:42,760
Today's Doggy

10
00:01:47,140 --> 00:01:48,260
Alright, today we're here.

11
00:01:48,260 --> 00:01:51,340
This is a report from a sauna just for dogs.

12
00:01:52,660 --> 00:01:55,200
It looks like it's relaxing and enjoying itself,
doesn't it?

13
00:01:56,220 --> 00:01:58,100
Well then, let's ask for its impressions.

14
00:01:58,680 --> 00:02:01,280
Buddy-chan, how are you feeling?

15
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:04,120
It says it feels wonderful.

16
00:02:04,980 --> 00:02:06,680
A sauna for a dog? What's this nonsense?

17
00:02:07,180 --> 00:02:08,840
After this, Buddy-chan will

18
00:02:08,840 --> 00:02:11,620
get pampered at a spa just for dogs,

19
00:02:12,180 --> 00:02:15,660
then enjoy a luxurious meal
at a dog-only restaurant,

20
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:19,820
and then spend the
night at a dog-only hotel.

21
00:02:20,620 --> 00:02:21,300
What did you say?

22
00:02:21,720 --> 00:02:23,860
How about that? Jealous, aren't you?

23
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:25,600
Of course I am, damn it.

24
00:02:30,680 --> 00:02:33,840
Senpai, please don't get so worked up.

25
00:02:34,520 --> 00:02:37,860
Hey, it's just a dog. Is it really
okay for it to live in such luxury?

26
00:02:38,300 --> 00:02:41,720
As a pet owner,
he's more like family than a dog.

27
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:45,820
My Sarah and I are going
to Hawaii starting tomorrow.

28
00:02:46,480 --> 00:02:47,960
A dog going to Hawaii?

29
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:52,060
Yes, we're entering a dog
contest held over there.

30
00:02:52,060 --> 00:02:54,300
Sarah is a top contender to win, you know.

31
00:02:55,020 --> 00:02:57,060
Are dogs even allowed to ride on airplanes?

32
00:02:57,700 --> 00:03:00,620
Services that attract
customers keep increasing.

33
00:03:01,340 --> 00:03:04,000
Our airline allows pets too.

34
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:06,460
As for me...

35
00:03:07,620 --> 00:03:09,220
The dorm bath broke down,

36
00:03:09,620 --> 00:03:13,580
so I'm out in the dorm yard in this freezing sky,
doing cold-water washing.

37
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:16,420
Ooh, amazing.

38
00:03:17,400 --> 00:03:20,540
I have no money for a haircut,
so my hair's a mess.

39
00:03:21,120 --> 00:03:24,420
I haven't eaten steak in years, you know!

40
00:03:27,920 --> 00:03:30,700
The dog's living a way better life than me,
you know!

41
00:03:32,160 --> 00:03:33,780
Poor old me.

42
00:03:34,640 --> 00:03:36,980
It's not as if that's
not Ryo-chan's own fault.

43
00:03:36,980 --> 00:03:39,800
In your case,
you can't really argue back, can you?

44
00:03:41,160 --> 00:03:42,900
What a cold thing to say.

45
00:03:42,900 --> 00:03:45,780
Buddy's living a better life than I am.

46
00:03:47,620 --> 00:03:49,600
I see. Well then -

47
00:03:50,920 --> 00:03:54,760
Reiko, before you head out tomorrow,
bring Sarah along.

48
00:03:54,760 --> 00:03:59,000
Fine, I'm meeting Komachi-chan
and the others here anyway.

49
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:02,300
Is that noisy one going along too?

50
00:04:02,300 --> 00:04:04,400
Yes, is there a problem with that?

51
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:07,700
Hey, no, it's nothing.

52
00:04:09,740 --> 00:04:12,120
Ryo-san's dog life.

53
00:04:14,740 --> 00:04:15,580
Good morning.

54
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:22,080
My, you've grown again, haven't you?

55
00:04:23,160 --> 00:04:23,800
There, there.

56
00:04:24,680 --> 00:04:26,580
She really takes to you, senpai.

57
00:04:26,580 --> 00:04:29,686
That's right,
he has a face that animals love.

58
00:04:29,736 --> 00:04:31,140
Ryo-chan, you know...

59
00:04:32,420 --> 00:04:34,240
Right, I'm taking her out for a little walk.

60
00:04:34,240 --> 00:04:36,220
Yeah, off you go.

61
00:04:36,920 --> 00:04:38,340
Alright, Sarah, let's go!

62
00:04:42,980 --> 00:04:44,180
Any moment now.

63
00:04:44,680 --> 00:04:45,900
She's here.

64
00:04:46,620 --> 00:04:47,340
Coming!

65
00:04:48,840 --> 00:04:50,220
Coming, Ryo-san.

66
00:04:50,220 --> 00:04:52,620
Bolbo...
Jodie, sorry for going out of your way.

67
00:04:54,080 --> 00:04:57,760
Alright, listen, Sarah. For two weeks,
you're switching places with me.

68
00:04:57,760 --> 00:05:00,120
Have Jodie look after you.

69
00:05:03,320 --> 00:05:06,180
Why are you disguising yourself as a dog,
Ryo-san?

70
00:05:07,940 --> 00:05:11,160
I thought I'd give Reiko a little surprise.

71
00:05:11,660 --> 00:05:13,020
But that's two weeks, you know.

72
00:05:14,820 --> 00:05:18,980
Jodie, if Americans worry about little things,
it's bad for your health.

73
00:05:19,940 --> 00:05:22,580
Come on, let's change.
Hurry up and close that door.

74
00:05:25,220 --> 00:05:30,620
Ryo-san,
are you really going through with this?

75
00:05:30,620 --> 00:05:35,120
Of course.
Dogs live a better life than I do.

76
00:05:35,120 --> 00:05:37,660
I want to live a life as good as a dog's.

77
00:05:37,660 --> 00:05:41,080
Eating gourmet food and relaxing in Hawaii.

78
00:05:41,740 --> 00:05:42,260
Sounds good.

79
00:05:43,020 --> 00:05:43,340
OK.

80
00:05:48,300 --> 00:05:50,180
Good! You really do look like a dog.

81
00:05:50,760 --> 00:05:52,380
I wonder if I can pull this off?

82
00:05:52,680 --> 00:05:56,380
Don't worry!
My acting is Academy Award-worthy.

83
00:05:57,140 --> 00:05:58,680
But your eyes look weird.

84
00:06:04,320 --> 00:06:05,740
Jodie, I'm borrowing this.

85
00:06:07,480 --> 00:06:08,580
Alright, this'll do.

86
00:06:09,860 --> 00:06:11,340
Well then, I'm counting on you.

87
00:06:14,600 --> 00:06:16,920
Reiko, sorry to keep you waiting.

88
00:06:17,780 --> 00:06:19,100
Welcome!

89
00:06:19,100 --> 00:06:20,780
Where's Sarah?

90
00:06:21,240 --> 00:06:23,440
Ryo-chan's taking her for a walk right now.

91
00:06:24,940 --> 00:06:26,020
They're back.

92
00:06:31,920 --> 00:06:33,980
Morubo-san, senpai?

93
00:06:33,980 --> 00:06:37,240
Well, I just ran into Ryotsu over there.

94
00:06:37,740 --> 00:06:40,680
He said he's taking some time off,
so he asked me to look after this dog.

95
00:06:41,140 --> 00:06:42,620
What? That's so irresponsible.

96
00:06:43,020 --> 00:06:46,680
He doesn't have a shred of responsibility.
He's the king of irresponsibility.

97
00:06:46,680 --> 00:06:48,840
After all, he is our senior.

98
00:06:49,260 --> 00:06:51,620
You guys, you'll pay for this later.

99
00:06:52,100 --> 00:06:54,780
Sarah, what happened to those sunglasses?

100
00:06:59,160 --> 00:07:05,300
Th-these? Ryotsu put them on her,
saying the sun in Hawaii must be strong.

101
00:07:05,860 --> 00:07:06,820
Ryo-chan did?

102
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:10,500
Well, Kankichi Ryotsu does
have a good side after all.

103
00:07:11,500 --> 00:07:13,520
Hey, Sarah seems to like them too.

104
00:07:14,420 --> 00:07:16,320
Good, nice save, Morubo.

105
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:20,400
Those sunglasses suit her, too.

106
00:07:20,400 --> 00:07:21,880
So cute.

107
00:07:29,460 --> 00:07:33,120
Wow, my first time ever in first class!

108
00:07:33,120 --> 00:07:35,080
So becoming a dog finally paid off.

109
00:07:35,080 --> 00:07:36,960
I have mixed feelings somehow.

110
00:07:37,640 --> 00:07:41,000
Maybe it's just my mood, but the
stewardesses are about 20% prettier too.

111
00:07:41,500 --> 00:07:41,680
Just...

112
00:07:42,460 --> 00:07:45,320
Look, look!
The ship looks so tiny from up here.

113
00:07:45,320 --> 00:07:47,140
It really looks like a toy.

114
00:07:47,780 --> 00:07:50,440
Those two being so loud is a bit of a flaw,
sometimes.

115
00:07:52,780 --> 00:07:53,300
Yes.

116
00:07:56,260 --> 00:07:57,660
I was surprised.

117
00:07:57,660 --> 00:07:59,720
That dog has a pedigree, you know.

118
00:07:59,720 --> 00:08:00,880
No way.

119
00:08:00,880 --> 00:08:01,740
It's true.

120
00:08:01,740 --> 00:08:06,140
Sorry to keep you waiting.

121
00:08:07,360 --> 00:08:07,880
Yes.

122
00:08:09,760 --> 00:08:10,720
It's true.

123
00:08:13,140 --> 00:08:15,720
Sarah, what are you doing?

124
00:08:19,780 --> 00:08:21,620
She seems kind of jittery.

125
00:08:22,780 --> 00:08:24,640
Aren't you just nervous?

126
00:08:25,080 --> 00:08:26,740
I'm sure that's it.

127
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:31,160
The real fun starts once we get there

128
00:08:45,860 --> 00:08:47,820
This is our room.

129
00:08:48,760 --> 00:08:49,640
Wow!

130
00:08:49,640 --> 00:08:50,580
Luxurious!

131
00:08:50,580 --> 00:08:53,700
Yes! This is how it should be.

132
00:08:54,560 --> 00:08:55,260
Tired?

133
00:08:55,500 --> 00:08:57,820
I really want to go swimming right away.

134
00:08:57,820 --> 00:09:00,820
Alright, that's settled.
Let's change right here.

135
00:09:03,460 --> 00:09:06,020
This is an unexpected showtime.

136
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:27,420
The sea! The sea! The sea!

137
00:09:27,940 --> 00:09:30,020
Sarah's so happy, look at her go.

138
00:09:30,020 --> 00:09:32,720
I've been to Hawaii five times,
but I've never seen this before.

139
00:09:34,520 --> 00:09:38,520
This is the best! I never thought
I'd get to come to Hawaii for free!

140
00:09:38,520 --> 00:09:40,720
Dog's life, woohoo!

141
00:09:40,720 --> 00:09:43,400
Wow, Sarah's doing the backstroke!

142
00:09:43,400 --> 00:09:45,540
Of course, she's Reiko's dog.

143
00:09:45,540 --> 00:09:48,420
When did she learn to do the backstroke?

144
00:09:51,060 --> 00:09:52,800
Dog surfing?

145
00:09:54,320 --> 00:09:57,680
That's right! You have to win! Give it here!

146
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:00,480
This is surfing, right!

147
00:10:00,760 --> 00:10:02,900
Yeah! It's surfing!

148
00:10:03,600 --> 00:10:05,340
Look! It's the Pipeline!

149
00:10:05,960 --> 00:10:07,960
Sarah! She's surfing!

150
00:10:08,160 --> 00:10:08,920
No way?

151
00:10:09,600 --> 00:10:13,080
Don't be so surprised by surfing.
I'm better at this.

152
00:10:15,860 --> 00:10:16,580
Sea!

153
00:10:21,060 --> 00:10:21,540
Go, go!

154
00:10:22,440 --> 00:10:24,680
Here I go! Aerial flip!

155
00:10:26,460 --> 00:10:27,140
Go!

156
00:10:27,580 --> 00:10:28,700
Yahoo!

157
00:10:29,220 --> 00:10:31,360
That's how you ride a jet ski!

158
00:10:31,900 --> 00:10:32,760
Alright!

159
00:10:33,720 --> 00:10:35,940
Sarah is so active!

160
00:10:36,300 --> 00:10:38,360
Her riding style reminds me of someone.

161
00:10:38,760 --> 00:10:40,020
Whoa!

162
00:10:40,060 --> 00:10:42,460
There are so many reporters here!

163
00:10:42,640 --> 00:10:45,360
A jet ski dog is pretty rare, isn't it?

164
00:10:45,800 --> 00:10:46,580
Woof woof woof!

165
00:10:46,580 --> 00:10:47,120
Nana-woof!

166
00:10:48,160 --> 00:10:48,640
Woof!

167
00:10:48,940 --> 00:10:49,000
Woof!

168
00:10:49,080 --> 00:10:49,460
Woof!

169
00:10:49,460 --> 00:10:49,800
Woof!

170
00:10:49,800 --> 00:10:50,080
Woof!

171
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:52,320
No way

172
00:10:52,320 --> 00:10:53,060
Aaaaaaah!

173
00:11:17,540 --> 00:11:20,140
A stray dog searching for food

174
00:11:20,140 --> 00:11:23,960
My status is different from you lot.
Fuhahaha!

175
00:11:25,800 --> 00:11:26,820
Good morning.

176
00:11:27,620 --> 00:11:28,060
Alright.

177
00:11:35,740 --> 00:11:38,020
Golf's amazing too, yude-mae!

178
00:11:38,020 --> 00:11:40,140
I've never taught that, you know.

179
00:11:43,060 --> 00:11:45,560
So this is how a rich man's dog lives.

180
00:11:47,540 --> 00:11:50,280
This is the rich life I've been longing for.

181
00:11:50,780 --> 00:11:52,380
Sunshine everywhere!

182
00:12:05,540 --> 00:12:07,440
I'm already sick of steak.

183
00:12:08,040 --> 00:12:09,900
I want something light and refreshing.

184
00:12:14,580 --> 00:12:16,100
You want Japanese food?

185
00:12:16,920 --> 00:12:19,100
Yay! Japanese food!

186
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:21,960
The chilled tofu is so good!

187
00:12:22,220 --> 00:12:24,280
After all, we Japanese really love washoku!

188
00:12:24,620 --> 00:12:26,260
The yakitori and sashimi are delicious too!

189
00:12:26,260 --> 00:12:27,900
The natto and stew are delicious too!

190
00:12:32,740 --> 00:12:34,080
And beer to finish!

191
00:12:38,640 --> 00:12:39,340
It's kicking in!

192
00:12:40,740 --> 00:12:42,900
It's hitting me...
I'm getting a little woozy.

193
00:12:49,740 --> 00:12:52,700
You fell asleep.
You're acting like an old man.

194
00:13:06,600 --> 00:13:09,280
The beer went right through me,
and now I need to pee!

195
00:13:13,480 --> 00:13:15,940
Oh no, I forgot I'm still
wearing this dog costume!

196
00:13:30,460 --> 00:13:34,320
Good girl, you peed in the toilet properly.

197
00:13:38,820 --> 00:13:40,140
W-what?

198
00:13:40,740 --> 00:13:42,680
What's wrong, Reiko?

199
00:13:42,680 --> 00:13:44,400
Sarah's acting strange.

200
00:13:44,400 --> 00:13:45,360
Sarah?

201
00:13:45,920 --> 00:13:47,720
Her fur's all gritty.

202
00:13:48,920 --> 00:13:51,300
Oh no, what's going to
happen to the contest?

203
00:13:53,480 --> 00:13:56,540
Not sheared, is she?

204
00:13:57,900 --> 00:14:02,620
What, nothing's wrong at all!
Really, thank goodness.

205
00:14:03,520 --> 00:14:09,080
Don't keep us in suspense, Reiko!
Sorry, I think I got the wrong idea.

206
00:14:10,100 --> 00:14:13,560
That was close. I let my guard down.

207
00:14:14,500 --> 00:14:16,480
Anyway, good night, Sarah.

208
00:14:20,500 --> 00:14:21,220
Heavy

209
00:14:24,640 --> 00:14:26,760
Sarah, haven't you gained weight?

210
00:14:27,680 --> 00:14:31,100
Well, ever since we got here,
all she's done is eat.

211
00:14:31,920 --> 00:14:33,760
And we have a contest coming up.

212
00:14:34,540 --> 00:14:37,120
Sarah, you're going on
a diet starting tomorrow.

213
00:14:39,560 --> 00:14:40,700
Acting cute won't work.

214
00:14:42,780 --> 00:14:43,820
Crying won't work either.

215
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:49,020
Come on, come on, Sarah. What's wrong?

216
00:14:49,020 --> 00:14:50,640
Your legs are so heavy.

217
00:14:50,640 --> 00:14:52,720
You only just started running again,
didn't you?

218
00:14:54,180 --> 00:14:55,340
Don't say that.

219
00:14:55,340 --> 00:14:57,800
Running at this school is tough, you know.

220
00:14:57,800 --> 00:15:00,060
Let's run as far as that palm tree.

221
00:15:02,980 --> 00:15:04,300
Yes, yes, keep it up.

222
00:15:04,300 --> 00:15:05,240
You can do it.

223
00:15:17,700 --> 00:15:19,140
What on earth has gotten into her?

224
00:15:19,140 --> 00:15:21,960
Looks like there's no
way she'll win like this.

225
00:15:22,540 --> 00:15:25,980
It's a shame,
since winning would get us $100,000.

226
00:15:28,340 --> 00:15:30,540
If she wins, it's $100,000.

227
00:15:37,500 --> 00:16:03,040
Uuuuuuuugh...

228
00:16:03,040 --> 00:16:05,560
This dog seems to have changed.

229
00:16:13,680 --> 00:16:14,700
No way.

230
00:16:16,040 --> 00:16:16,620
Sarah!

231
00:16:17,740 --> 00:16:18,500
Come here.

232
00:16:19,660 --> 00:16:21,440
So the master's calling, is he?

233
00:16:25,720 --> 00:16:28,200
Sarah was good at handstands, wasn't she?

234
00:16:29,620 --> 00:16:30,360
Handstands.

235
00:16:31,620 --> 00:16:32,920
Come on, hurry!

236
00:16:33,720 --> 00:16:35,300
That's easy.

237
00:16:35,300 --> 00:16:38,240
If we get caught here,
the $100,000 is down the drain.

238
00:16:40,560 --> 00:16:42,800
And then the moonwalk backflip.

239
00:16:50,380 --> 00:16:53,860
And the Yokai face-first reverse drop, too.

240
00:16:58,020 --> 00:16:59,780
Spinning a trout on an umbrella.

241
00:17:01,220 --> 00:17:02,120
And the Hayadori, too.

242
00:17:03,320 --> 00:17:04,500
Even lace knitting!

243
00:17:12,600 --> 00:17:14,020
So that's what happened.

244
00:17:14,020 --> 00:17:15,140
Ryo-chan.

245
00:17:21,580 --> 00:17:23,520
Reiko, I'm so sorry.

246
00:17:23,520 --> 00:17:26,260
I just got it out of Bobby.

247
00:17:26,680 --> 00:17:28,980
Sarah's staying with me, so

248
00:17:28,980 --> 00:17:29,880
don't worry.

249
00:17:30,900 --> 00:17:32,060
Yes, see you later.

250
00:17:34,380 --> 00:17:36,280
How did it go, Reiko?

251
00:17:36,660 --> 00:17:37,920
Just as I thought.

252
00:17:37,920 --> 00:17:40,280
Sarah was at Jodie's place.

253
00:17:40,900 --> 00:17:44,400
So that gorilla guy
really was posing as Sarah.

254
00:17:44,400 --> 00:17:45,560
I can't forgive that.

255
00:17:46,560 --> 00:17:48,940
Yes, let's give him a good punishment.

256
00:17:49,420 --> 00:17:50,120
How?

257
00:17:50,900 --> 00:17:52,320
Well, tomorrow...

258
00:18:06,140 --> 00:18:06,520
Mm.

259
00:18:06,520 --> 00:18:08,040
Isn't it here?

260
00:18:26,680 --> 00:18:29,140
They all look like tough competition.

261
00:18:32,120 --> 00:18:35,620
Ladies and gentlemen,
thank you for your long wait.

262
00:18:35,620 --> 00:18:39,200
The official dog contest
is finally about to begin!

263
00:18:39,600 --> 00:18:41,540
The brave warriors gathered on this ground,

264
00:18:41,540 --> 00:18:44,340
which of these dogs will win the glory?

265
00:18:50,420 --> 00:18:51,980
Now, the first round is

266
00:18:52,800 --> 00:18:55,980
a speed-eating contest
for Super Tokumori Dog Food!

267
00:18:55,980 --> 00:18:58,700
Whether it's dog food or cat food,

268
00:18:58,700 --> 00:19:01,200
I can't take it,
not with $100,000 on the line!

269
00:19:01,660 --> 00:19:03,260
He's eating dog food!

270
00:19:03,260 --> 00:19:04,920
And it looks delicious, too.

271
00:19:08,980 --> 00:19:11,920
Only Zakken No.
22, Sarah, held on at the top.

272
00:19:11,920 --> 00:19:13,820
Next, No. 18, Liger.

273
00:19:13,820 --> 00:19:16,020
No. 50, Thunder Debris,
is chasing after them.

274
00:19:16,440 --> 00:19:18,360
Now, what's the next event?

275
00:19:19,300 --> 00:19:19,980
Sit like a squirrel!

276
00:19:20,920 --> 00:19:21,640
Spin!

277
00:19:23,220 --> 00:19:24,120
Circus!

278
00:19:25,360 --> 00:19:27,460
Here, your sense of balance will be tested.

279
00:19:27,460 --> 00:19:29,280
Can they make it across
the single-plank bridge?

280
00:19:30,080 --> 00:19:32,640
Next, the 360-degree giant rotating course!

281
00:19:32,640 --> 00:19:35,380
It's a hailstorm of dropouts!

282
00:19:36,140 --> 00:19:37,380
Stepping-stone trap

283
00:19:37,380 --> 00:19:41,200
Step wrong and the
punching gloves will attack!

284
00:19:41,960 --> 00:19:42,820
Barrel toss

285
00:19:42,820 --> 00:19:44,260
No. 22, Sarah

286
00:19:44,260 --> 00:19:45,800
Clear this with flying colors

287
00:19:46,380 --> 00:19:47,680
And then, the inferno

288
00:19:49,560 --> 00:19:51,300
Can you get through while dodging?

289
00:19:52,800 --> 00:19:55,040
You're moving much more
like a dog than any real dog!

290
00:19:55,780 --> 00:19:59,060
It's because he believes
he'll get $100,000 if he wins.

291
00:19:59,520 --> 00:20:01,720
Greed is what drives Ryo-chan, after all.

292
00:20:01,720 --> 00:20:06,740
Now, the next challenge:
a dive from this 300-meter cliff!

293
00:20:06,740 --> 00:20:13,640
And then, the super-difficult one: dive 300 meters with the
sumo team and bring back a treasure chest from the seabed.

294
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:25,440
Do I jump from here?

295
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:28,960
I'm not giving up now
that I've come this far!

296
00:20:28,960 --> 00:20:30,660
It's for the $100,000.

297
00:20:31,420 --> 00:20:32,460
$100,000!

298
00:20:33,240 --> 00:20:36,620
As expected, Number 22,
Sarah, dove in first.

299
00:20:36,620 --> 00:20:39,080
The other dogs follow suit.

300
00:20:41,420 --> 00:20:43,500
Can he hold his breath for 300 meters?

301
00:20:44,940 --> 00:20:47,240
Except for Sarah, the other dogs
failed to hit the water cleanly.

302
00:20:47,240 --> 00:20:49,040
They're out here.

303
00:20:53,320 --> 00:20:55,500
I'm starting to run out of breath!

304
00:20:56,580 --> 00:20:57,740
There it is.

305
00:20:58,780 --> 00:21:00,220
If I don't have shiso...

306
00:21:05,720 --> 00:21:07,160
I can't take it anymore.

307
00:21:07,920 --> 00:21:10,240
What's wrong, Sarah?

308
00:21:10,240 --> 00:21:11,640
She still hasn't come up.

309
00:21:11,640 --> 00:21:14,720
As expected, it's a 300-meter round trip,
600 meters in total.

310
00:21:14,720 --> 00:21:16,380
Was it too much for her last week?

311
00:21:19,880 --> 00:21:22,780
Yeah, this dog really is different.

312
00:21:23,200 --> 00:21:27,940
It seems she snatched a regulator
from a diver nearby.

313
00:21:28,520 --> 00:21:31,220
Wow, in more ways than one,
this is an amazing dog.

314
00:21:32,480 --> 00:21:37,540
Can a dog really pull
off something like this?

315
00:21:38,480 --> 00:21:40,040
There she is!

316
00:21:40,860 --> 00:21:44,060
Overcoming countless trials, she alone

317
00:21:44,060 --> 00:21:47,820
is the last brave warrior
racing toward the glorious goal.

318
00:21:47,820 --> 00:21:50,360
Everyone, please welcome her
with a warm round of applause!

319
00:21:50,360 --> 00:21:52,780
A triumphant finish!

320
00:21:54,820 --> 00:21:56,140
I actually won.

321
00:21:56,140 --> 00:21:58,520
I can't believe it.

322
00:21:59,120 --> 00:22:03,480
Now, the winner, Sarah,
has a wonderful prize waiting for her!

323
00:22:03,480 --> 00:22:05,820
Sarah, are you ready?

324
00:22:06,360 --> 00:22:09,200
Yes! I got the $100,000!

325
00:22:09,760 --> 00:22:11,100
Wow, Ryo-chan!

326
00:22:11,100 --> 00:22:12,600
Stronger than a dog.

327
00:22:15,360 --> 00:22:16,460
How about that?

328
00:22:16,460 --> 00:22:19,980
You all knew it was me?

329
00:22:19,980 --> 00:22:23,240
Congratulations on winning!

330
00:22:23,240 --> 00:22:27,580
You have been chosen as the
world's first space exploration dog.

331
00:22:27,580 --> 00:22:29,460
Please go and do your best.

332
00:22:30,100 --> 00:22:31,560
Na-na-na-na-na!

333
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:50,920
Wait, I'm a human!

334
00:22:54,240 --> 00:22:56,480
Take care, Ryo-chan!

335
00:22:56,780 --> 00:22:57,680
Bye-bye!

336
00:23:25,380 --> 00:23:27,720
I'm home, Sarah. Have you been a good girl?

337
00:23:28,380 --> 00:23:30,080
Yes, she's been very good.

338
00:23:30,080 --> 00:23:32,720
Much better than our Bobby, for sure.

339
00:23:34,500 --> 00:23:35,540
Sorry.

340
00:23:37,200 --> 00:23:40,260
By the way, I don't see Ryo-san anywhere.

341
00:23:41,500 --> 00:23:43,300
Ryo-chan is probably by now...

342
00:23:45,060 --> 00:23:45,520
That won't do.

343
00:23:47,940 --> 00:23:49,800
But I wonder if Ryo-chan is all right.

344
00:23:49,800 --> 00:23:52,420
He's fine. It's that gorilla guy.

345
00:23:52,420 --> 00:23:55,140
Right, Ryo-chan will be fine, won't he?

346
00:23:56,160 --> 00:23:57,600
As if he'd be fine.

347
00:23:58,420 --> 00:24:01,300
Just send him back to Earth already.

348
00:24:15,080 --> 00:24:27,040
As if someone were calling, on a afternoon after the rain,
I walked looking back, my hand held by Gaaja.

349
00:24:27,040 --> 00:24:34,180
That strange feeling I had back then

350
00:24:34,900 --> 00:24:39,460
So on the arcade's tiles,

351
00:24:39,460 --> 00:24:45,240
I tried walking only on the black ones.

352
00:24:47,600 --> 00:24:51,420
Everyone was a child once,

353
00:24:51,420 --> 00:24:53,560
but everyone has forgotten.

354
00:24:54,460 --> 00:24:57,540
Not with politicians with
their self-important faces,

355
00:24:57,540 --> 00:25:00,820
nor with aunties whose brows tremble.

356
00:25:01,360 --> 00:25:03,840
Go on, try turning

357
00:25:04,440 --> 00:25:06,420
at that corner.

358
00:25:07,440 --> 00:25:11,640
You'll get to meet everyone!

359
00:25:12,200 --> 00:25:16,260
Over there is Kameari,

360
00:25:17,280 --> 00:25:19,560
surely Kameari is there,

361
00:25:21,120 --> 00:25:24,820
everyone, come to our town,

362
00:25:25,940 --> 00:25:26,340
thank you.

363
00:25:30,880 --> 00:25:34,840
When I was a kid,
there weren't many tall buildings yet,

364
00:25:34,840 --> 00:25:38,020
and only the bathhouse chimneys
towered high in the sky.

365
00:25:38,020 --> 00:25:41,800
This is about the young aspiring
painter we met in those days

366
00:25:41,800 --> 00:25:43,880
and the memories we shared with her.

367
00:25:43,880 --> 00:25:47,480
Next time:
"Shitamachi Sentō Emaki." See you then!

368
00:25:51,640 --> 00:25:53,940
surely Kameari is there,

369
00:25:53,940 --> 00:25:59,140
everyone, come to our town,

370
00:25:59,980 --> 00:26:00,780
thank you.

